  <p class="crumbs"><a href={project}>← Governed Agentic Empirical Research</a></p>
  <h1>How agentic-governance works</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">The workflow inside, and where the human comes in</p>
  <p class="lede">
    agentic-governance is the operating system my repositories run on. It says how work is planned,
    classified, done, reviewed, merged and remembered, whether a person or an AI agent does it. The short
    version: agents can do almost all of the work. A human approves every change that alters meaning.
  </p>
  <p class="pin">
    Describes <a href={`${canon}/VERSION`}>v0.9.1</a> at commit <code>01c7d69</code>. This page is a summary.
    Where it and the <a href={`${canon}/llm/governance/`}>canonical documents</a> disagree, the documents win.
  </p>

  <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
    <a href="#layers">Three layers</a> ·
    <a href="#workflow">The workflow</a> ·
    <a href="#levels">Levels</a> ·
